From 7ebba06a30eaf08c10b26b28ca14bfee1c791576 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:48:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add conservative x86-64 BSR semantics and tests

[AGENT 2026-10-15] Model BSR for 16/32/64-bit operands using Nat.log2
for nonzero inputs. Preserve zero-input destinations, allowing either full
preservation or upper-half clearing for zero-input 32-bit operations.
Keep all five non-ZF arithmetic flags universally undefined. This covers
the current Intel and AMD specifications without excluding equal keys in
the WireGuard common_bits proof or assuming a particular CPU vendor.

References: Intel SDM rev089, volume2A page3-109 and its older-processor
footnotes; AMD APM24594 rev3.37, BSR. The older Intel wording quoted in
Linux's bitops.h has been superseded.
https://cdrdv2-public.intel.com/868137/325462-089-sdm-vol-1-2abcd-3abcd-4.pdf
https://docs.amd.com/api/khub/documents/j44LvPXzuuXgM0WyHKQfeQ/content

Add register/memory parsing, both printers, width/operand rejection tests,
26 executable guards, four AT&T round trips, two symbolic universal
execution tests, and a native assembly comparison. Both zero-W32 outcomes
are exercised; the native test avoids unspecified upper-half differences.

Validation (all heavy commands capped, toolchain selected per command with
ELAN_TOOLCHAIN=leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0):
- lake build: PASS, 68 jobs.
- lake build Kraken.X64.BsrTests: PASS; both printed axiom sets contain
  only propext, Classical.choice, and Quot.sound.
- lake env leanchecker --fresh Kraken.X64.BsrTests: PASS.
- python3 -B Kraken/X64/Test/asm_tests.py Kraken/X64/Test/asm/test_bsr.S:
  PASS, 1/1 native comparison.
- git diff --check: PASS.

Failed incidental invocation, not a pass: lake env leanchecker --help
ignored the unknown flag and attempted a broad check, then was KILLED
at the unchanged32GB cap (exit137). The subsequent fresh check above
has a different, explicit module scope. Development elaboration errors
in the new tests were corrected before the final passes.

AI provenance: Codex generated and locally reviewed the implementation,
tests, and this explanation. No generated source-code comments were
added. This private commit is not an upstream maintainer review or release.
